-- #1111 A-2.4 BYSTANDER FIXTURE -- "feature + UNRELATED code still behaves", which
-- is the shape AGENTS.md requires of any change that re-keys a PROGRAM-GLOBAL TABLE,
-- as opposed to "feature works".
--
-- A-2.4 re-keys `universeIfaceRequiredRef` (impl completeness) and
-- `universeIfaceParamKinds` (graded instance-head kinds) from a bare INTERFACE name
-- to a module-qualified identity.  The fixtures that prove the FEATURE are the
-- drained #1257/#1258 repros -- each asserts that a SHADOWED interface name now
-- resolves to the right module.  This fixture asserts the other half, which no
-- drained repro can: that a module which shadows NOTHING is checked exactly as it
-- would be with no collision in the graph at all.
--
-- The graph DOES contain a collision: `dupg.mdk` and `dupp.mdk` both declare an
-- interface `Same` at arity 1 -- one graded with required method `gandThen`, one
-- ungraded with required method `pmth`.  Only their unrelated FUNCTIONS are imported,
-- so both are registered into the cross-module universe and neither is nameable from
-- here.  NOTHING BELOW MENTIONS `Same`, `gandThen` OR `pmth`.
--
-- What the golden pins (every file's bucket is `[]`), and how each line can fail:
--   * `impl Own ET` implements BOTH of `Own`'s required methods.  If the completeness
--     lookup answered with the wrong interface's required-method list, this would
--     gain a T-INCOMPLETE-IMPL naming `gandThen` or `pmth` -- #1258's symptom on a
--     name that collides with nothing.
--   * `impl OwnGraded Asy` is CORRECTLY kinded: `OwnGraded`'s slot 0 is `Row` and
--     `Asy`'s slot 0 is `Row` too (`Unit -> <e> a` is what makes a param row-kinded).
--     If the slot-kind lookup answered with the wrong interface's slot kinds this
--     would gain a spurious T-IMPL-KIND-MISMATCH -- #1257's symptom, again on a
--     non-colliding name.
--   * `impl Display ET` is a BYSTANDER, not a witness -- the bullet here claimed it
--     was one ("a key that could not reach the prelude's own rows would break here
--     first") until adversarial review, which is a member of the very class the 🚨
--     paragraph below excludes, twelve lines further down its own header.  `Display`
--     has exactly one required method (`display`, stdlib/core.mdk), and this impl
--     defines it: a MISS gives `None => []`, a HIT gives required `["display"]` minus
--     defined `["display"]` = `[]`.  Byte-identical, so it can only ever pin that a
--     complete prelude impl stays quiet.  COUNTERFACTUAL, RUN: deleting
--     `insertIfaceRequired`'s `DInterface` arm -- killing the completeness registry
--     for every module -- leaves this whole fixture green and every bucket `[]`.
--     The REJECTING direction against a prelude interface is covered by
--     `test/analyze_project_fixtures/1111_a24_genuine_iface_rejects/`'s
--     `impl Ord GT2`, which was added because of this same review finding.
--   * `plain` mentions none of A-2.4's machinery at all -- it is here to answer
--     AGENTS.md's "what happens to a program that never touches the table" directly.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS FIXTURE CANNOT CATCH, stated so nobody reads it as covering more than
-- it does.  It detects a key that WRONGLY MEETS another module's row (a spurious
-- diagnostic appears).  It CANNOT detect a key that NEVER MEETS its own row: both
-- readers abstain on a miss, so a write-side/read-side key disagreement would leave
-- every bucket here `[]` and this fixture green while the checks had silently
-- stopped running.  That direction is covered by the mirror-probe fixtures instead:
-- `test/analyze_project_fixtures/1111_a24_genuine_iface_rejects/` covers BOTH tables
-- on the module arm (and, since this same review, core's own rows via `impl Ord
-- GT2`), and `test/typecheck_error_fixtures/graded_head_wrong_kind_flat.mdk` covers
-- `ifaceParamKindsRef` on the flat arm.  Each goes SILENT exactly when this one
-- cannot.  ⚠️ Its sibling `iface_incomplete_impl_flat.mdk` was listed here too and
-- does NOT belong: the FLAT arm routes completeness to the bare-name scan
-- `ifaceRequiredMethods`, never to the re-keyed registry, so it cannot go silent on
-- a key disagreement.  See that fixture's own corrected header.
-- The set is the assertion; no single member is.
import dupg.{dg}  -- ONLY the function; never dupg's Same
import dupp.{dp}  -- ONLY the function; never dupp's Same

interface Own a where
  ownFoo : a -> Int
  ownBar : a -> Int

data ET = MkET

impl Own ET where
  ownFoo e = 1
  ownBar e = 2

impl Display ET where
  display e = "ET"

interface OwnGraded (f : Effect -> Type -> Type) where
  ownThen : f e a -> (a -> <e> f e b) -> f e b

public export data Asy (e : Effect) a = MkAsy (Unit -> <e> a)

impl OwnGraded Asy where
  ownThen a f = ownThen a f

plain : Int -> Int
plain n = n + 1

n : Int
n = dg (dp (plain (ownFoo MkET + ownBar MkET)))
